WEBVTT

00:09:59.636 --> 00:10:01.036
"Oh, I need glasses."

00:10:01.076 --> 00:10:03.156
You show up in the kitchen
and you're like,

00:10:03.156 --> 00:10:05.556
"Am I hungry? Am I thirsty?"

00:10:05.556 --> 00:10:07.436
Because, right, the cues are signaling,

00:10:07.436 --> 00:10:08.996
"Is it a meal? Is it what?"

00:10:09.036 --> 00:10:11.156
And not the glasses
that you didn't notice.

00:10:11.196 --> 00:10:13.396
So when you walk
into the room and you're like,

00:10:13.436 --> 00:10:15.316
"I don't know why I'm here,"

00:10:15.356 --> 00:10:17.956
you're not going crazy,
you're not getting Alzheimer's,

00:10:17.956 --> 00:10:19.836
your memory isn't terrible.

00:10:19.876 --> 00:10:24.236
It's, go back to the room you were in
before you landed in this one,

00:10:24.236 --> 00:10:26.676
either in your mind's eye
or physically do it

00:10:26.676 --> 00:10:30.556
and imagine the cues that were there
and it will instantly deliver